      "body": "## Motivation\n\nRegression coverage for #43094. With a cache-agnostic policy (`fcfs`, `lof`, `random`, `routing-key`), `calc_priority` skips the sort-time prefix match, so the admission re-match in `Req.init_next_round_input` is the only place these requests record `num_matched_prefix_tokens`. Before #42823 that re-match never wrote the field. Every request kept 0 while still reusing cached prefixes, so load snapshots (`get_num_waiting_uncached_tokens`) and cache-hit reporting read zero reuse: a 30-minute fcfs replay reported 0 matched tokens against a 91.6% token-weighted hit rate.\n\n#42823 fixed this by recording the match length inside `match_kv_cache`, but no test asserts it for the admission path. These tests guard against a refactor of `match_kv_cache` / `init_next_round_input` silently dropping that write again.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`test/registered/unit/managers/test_schedule_policy.py`: `TestAdmissionMatchedPrefixTokens`, three CPU cases on a simulated radix tree that holds a 64-token prefix.\n- `test_warm_req_records_match_length`: a request sharing the prefix records 64 at admission.\n- `test_cold_req_records_zero`: a request that shares no tokens with the cached prefix records 0, so the write does not count unrelated tokens.\n- `test_rematch_after_retraction_records_again`: `reset_for_retract()` zeroes the field, and the next admission re-match records 64 again.\n\nTest-only; no runtime change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable (test-only).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable (test-only).\n\n**Unit tests** (CPU, on current main `f77064f635`):\n- `python3 test/registered/unit/managers/test_schedule_policy.py`: 14 tests OK (3 new, 11 existing).\n- With the #42823 write in `match_kv_cache` removed (`req.num_matched_prefix_tokens = min(...)`), the warm and retraction cases fail with `0 != 64`, and the cold case still passes as intended.\n- `pre-commit run --files test/registered/unit/managers/test_schedule_policy.py`: all hooks pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41600049008](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41600049008)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41600048422](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41600048422)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41600048522](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41600048522)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
